{"name":"Shy Candela","hex":"#d6dde6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tachawit. The native name for the Shawiya language."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily frightened; timid.","Reserved; disinclined to familiar approach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shy"},{"term":"candela","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In the International System of Units, the base unit of luminous intensity; the luminous intensity, in a given direction, of a source that emits monochromatic radiation of frequency 540 × 10 hertz and that has a radiant intensity in that direction of 1/683 watt per steradian. Symbol: cd"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candela"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shyness","blocks":[{"text":"Shyness is a psychological trait characterized by social inhibition and apprehension in response to new social environments or perceived social judgement. It is frequently associated with social avoidance. Although shyness can be an attribute of people who have low self-esteem, the trait is often defined by a concern regarding the negative evaluation of others, such as mocking or rejection. While shyness is considered a normal personality variant, it is distinct from clinical conditions such as social anxiety disorder, which involves impairment in daily functioning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/20220801_Introversion_-_Shyness_-_Social_anxiety_disorder_-_comparative_chart.svg/330px-20220801_Introversion_-_Shyness_-_Social_anxiety_disorder_-_comparative_chart.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shyness"},{"title":"Candela","blocks":[{"text":"Candela is the SI unit of luminous intensity. It measures the luminous power per unit solid angle emitted in a particular direction. A common wax candle has a luminous intensity of roughly 1 cd."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Luminosity.svg/330px-Luminosity.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candela"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg/500px-Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg/1280px-Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg/500px-Group_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Putting one's hand over their mouth while laughing is often seen as an example of shyness in certain cultures (first child), as is hiding behind somebody else's back (third child)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGroup_of_children_in_a_village_in_West_Bengal%2C_Purba_Bardhaman.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/BlackBody.jpg/330px-BlackBody.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/BlackBody.jpg/330px-BlackBody.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1=radiating tube of thorium dioxide; 2=melting pot; 3=solidifying platinum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlackBody.jpg"}],"sounds":{"shy":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm